=⟨3,6,-1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 3+7\\cdot 6+0\\cdot (-1)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{7}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{\\sqrt{50}\\cdot \\sqrt{46}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{\\sqrt{2300}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{10\\sqrt{23}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{39}{10\\sqrt{23}})≈{35.6}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-67797/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-67797"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124802/selection/6ce441abfe5f67d73840f60b516fb56d654b803457c83f13ff883367ccae5efd" :answer/id #uuid "c716782a-b97a-58c3-aa44-b66192a533c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{53}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124802/selection/9065e450684baa8e61df08be51d6ad4312af70399bfb3dc0e200b2a0d7963b7b" :answer/id #uuid "deb98318-2cd0-59c5-8f0f-fb8177d23a14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{48}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124802/selection/b84d516698a1be204527297a088cf90216a400178e15b5cece027ef82c083708" :answer/id #uuid "98e25aad-57ef-55a6-89e1-0626f079d3e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{57}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124802/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" :answer/id #uuid "5864358b-e236-53ba-b047-be2a74903070" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124802/selection/e18a4ca1e21416a06996f4e4fb49519cd15fc99924d4291591f2019669983c5e" :answer/id #uuid "7ef2feb2-578c-5cf5-aa04-624fa071db91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124802/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "10fb002f-9c68-5e0d-8422-8879351ebc22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124802/selection/e18a4ca1e21416a06996f4e4fb49519cd15fc99924d4291591f2019669983c5e" :answer-field/choices ["q-124802/selection/6ce441abfe5f67d73840f60b516fb56d654b803457c83f13ff883367ccae5efd" "q-124802/selection/9065e450684baa8e61df08be51d6ad4312af70399bfb3dc0e200b2a0d7963b7b" "q-124802/selection/b84d516698a1be204527297a088cf90216a400178e15b5cece027ef82c083708" "q-124802/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" "q-124802/selection/e18a4ca1e21416a06996f4e4fb49519cd15fc99924d4291591f2019669983c5e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124802" :question/id #uuid "6b08cdc2-93c5-5479-9a26-db3836e3a1c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-124802" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=⟨3,1,1⟩$ and $b=⟨1,3,1⟩.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{11}\\cdot \\sqrt{11}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{7}{11})≈{50}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124802/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124802"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-124813"] :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,2⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-5,1⟩,\\,c=⟨1,-4,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-5,1⟩-⟨2,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-4,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨1,-4,-1⟩-⟨2,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot (-3)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{18}\\cdot \\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3\\sqrt{38}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{14}{3\\sqrt{38}})≈{41}^{∘}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-101511"] :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,1,-2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,1,-2⟩-⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,2,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,1⟩-⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{182}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{182}})≈{86}^{∘}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-19110"] :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨0,4,5⟩,\\,q=⟨1,5,4⟩,\\,r=⟨2,3,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨1,5,4⟩-⟨0,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨2,3,6⟩-⟨0,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(0)={90}^{∘}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-124826/selection/8c67eea01d8938bcf5b5511867d2afa0fc68682ba237ff8b210de282b2bc64f4" :answer/id #uuid "0efd139f-2138-5c6a-8e89-f0113b4b5529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124826/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" :answer/id #uuid "77dbf72a-adae-5231-b827-7a1763244fb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124826/selection/9342b0c907fb602c00c73ecf16b05da1e439ae387b93d6fd5bcfe7d47fe1bc14" :answer/id #uuid "5e90994a-68d7-554e-8846-e8e826dcaf09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{28}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124826/selection/e72de562c7b6e499859099a87925b9e505257e3ffa864de9eb0228a0ffe3652e" :answer/id #uuid "a49f55ad-0b4a-59d1-9d05-998e90849253" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{21}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124826/selection/0e0ca97cb22143426432e2e93582a8f181eca7b060b10d6f4f505538bf597a11" :answer/id #uuid "b799d246-a11b-5070-8463-6dd43a31f2fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{23}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124826/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "45442419-9910-5c12-9801-3473e30f7e7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124826/selection/8c67eea01d8938bcf5b5511867d2afa0fc68682ba237ff8b210de282b2bc64f4" :answer-field/choices ["q-124826/selection/8c67eea01d8938bcf5b5511867d2afa0fc68682ba237ff8b210de282b2bc64f4" "q-124826/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" "q-124826/selection/9342b0c907fb602c00c73ecf16b05da1e439ae387b93d6fd5bcfe7d47fe1bc14" "q-124826/selection/e72de562c7b6e499859099a87925b9e505257e3ffa864de9eb0228a0ffe3652e" "q-124826/selection/0e0ca97cb22143426432e2e93582a8f181eca7b060b10d6f4f505538bf597a11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124826" :question/id #uuid "2da436d8-ed5e-54f6-ba9e-01977eb421f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-124826" :question/problem "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-2,1,0)$, $Y(-1,0,4)$, and $Z(-1,2,-2).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-2,1,0⟩,\\,y=⟨-1,0,4⟩,\\,z=⟨-1,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,0⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,4⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{40}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{240}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{4\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}})={25}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124826/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124826"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-19112"] :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(3,-3,1)$, $B(5,-3,3)$, and $C(3,-2,3).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨3,-3,1⟩,\\,b=⟨5,-3,3⟩,\\,c=⟨3,-2,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨5,-3,3⟩-⟨3,-3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,3⟩-⟨3,-3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}})≈{51}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-101520"] :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $D$, $E$, $F$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d=⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩,\\,e=⟨{t}^{2},\\,2,\\,t⟩,\\,f=⟨t+3,\\,{t}^{2},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△DEF$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠EDF=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/c9cfb3e84e6f76d243125f2a09246b2a1300a0134e71359bb2b528082f064f93.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,2,\\,t⟩-⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2}-t,\\,-3,\\,t-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =⟨t+3,\\,{t}^{2},\\,1⟩-⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,{t}^{2}-5,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=6$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =6 \\\\ ({t}^{2}-t)\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot ({t}^{2}-5)+(t-3)\\cdot (-2) & =6 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-3t-3{t}^{2}+15-2t+6 & =6 \\\\ -5t+21 & =6 \\\\ -5t & =-15 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨{3}^{2}-3,-3,3-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-3,0⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨3,{3}^{2}-5,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,4,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}}{|\\overset{\\to }{DE}||\\overset{\\to }{DF}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{29}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{145}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{145}})≈{80.44}^{∘}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-77167/selection/30f153d44f656adcbbd73b17a5319fd295b089439ea8448b1e07507b88846e84" :answer/id #uuid "f974f885-0f17-5500-a7fe-b3bd99079839" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{21.42}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77167/selection/fcd8e7e744375c4711f5edb5f3724c6578da623e2bad6ae0f2fd450e82251159" :answer/id #uuid "be57eafa-5a3e-5467-8488-646d3a30fbca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{10.52}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77167/selection/773793c0669df614f2c269f494c5dc39f9dbff6b223a84912488c0a7719d6582" :answer/id #uuid "c52c118f-55a2-5a15-92a7-015727f1d9f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{77.07}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77167/selection/264cb7af50412d85fe80e9bf6625824cd333a129fae2d446fd6cf6f2c5df5de6" :answer/id #uuid "6d72837a-6c83-5f35-929e-ffa5344f19be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{63.43}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77167/selection/83c2f62318c9e858db7c0d2ec149a2741f8cd757c6e6eecd931a3d0beb3574ad" :answer/id #uuid "38a10d4d-48eb-58bc-ab1d-69d971c1060c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{26.57}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77167/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "43f81a4f-4f23-590d-a87a-a991a42d8c5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77167/selection/83c2f62318c9e858db7c0d2ec149a2741f8cd757c6e6eecd931a3d0beb3574ad" :answer-field/choices ["q-77167/selection/30f153d44f656adcbbd73b17a5319fd295b089439ea8448b1e07507b88846e84" "q-77167/selection/fcd8e7e744375c4711f5edb5f3724c6578da623e2bad6ae0f2fd450e82251159" "q-77167/selection/773793c0669df614f2c269f494c5dc39f9dbff6b223a84912488c0a7719d6582" "q-77167/selection/264cb7af50412d85fe80e9bf6625824cd333a129fae2d446fd6cf6f2c5df5de6" "q-77167/selection/83c2f62318c9e858db7c0d2ec149a2741f8cd757c6e6eecd931a3d0beb3574ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77167" :question/id #uuid "e36ca8d6-b65d-5cd3-83a7-070f0b3504a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-77167" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(2t,4,3),$ $B(5t-1,4,3)$ and $C(2t+4,t+5,3).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=8.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩,\\,b=⟨5t-1,\\,4,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨2t+4,\\,t+5,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨5t-1,\\,4,\\,3⟩-⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3t-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨2t+4,\\,t+5,\\,3⟩-⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,t+1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=8,$ we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =8 \\\\ (3t-1)\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (t+1)+0\\cdot 0 & =8 \\\\ 4(3t-1)+0+0 & =8 \\\\ 12t-4 & =8 \\\\ 12t & =12 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,0,0⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{80}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}})≈{26.57}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-77167/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77167"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-77164"] :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩,\\,b=⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3t,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2$, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =2 \\\\ 0\\cdot 2t+3t\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1 & =2 \\\\ 3t-1 & =2 \\\\ 3t & =3 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨0,3,-1⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}})≈{75}^{∘}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-19040/selection/23333e927931c238005cd6b80d3a6c712eecb716890a82ef4cb866488870a330" :answer/id #uuid "c7ae5663-0d59-5cf2-a70b-62b42701ed37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{87.33}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19040/selection/c231a711cbe815a3f97b63377b69824fc102bde5a6b290c0102af0fecad51e54" :answer/id #uuid "65a41328-671f-5e00-8c6d-3e0ed7c56e07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{72.34}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19040/selection/2b70365b330e910b66988567c99a87adc47bd52821686406cba25dc409452013" :answer/id #uuid "f8c57a36-dbd9-5114-a664-b21e93edfecc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{88.21}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19040/selection/35188f27c522133f17bcfbd3c4cc9c0d2dd0653aa8a22678fbd9e0ec70e87a62" :answer/id #uuid "28c08126-cfd7-5626-9ae8-efab8abd2d87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{81.33}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19040/selection/f89dce3f749fcbecd74cfcf45917bb3f72c9e5d9702d9a02ba2a060b4187e84a" :answer/id #uuid "46a9a117-bce4-54bb-952d-4a280afe930e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{67.13}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19040/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c8876ef-878d-5529-9fcb-4f967104239f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19040/selection/35188f27c522133f17bcfbd3c4cc9c0d2dd0653aa8a22678fbd9e0ec70e87a62" :answer-field/choices ["q-19040/selection/23333e927931c238005cd6b80d3a6c712eecb716890a82ef4cb866488870a330" "q-19040/selection/c231a711cbe815a3f97b63377b69824fc102bde5a6b290c0102af0fecad51e54" "q-19040/selection/2b70365b330e910b66988567c99a87adc47bd52821686406cba25dc409452013" "q-19040/selection/35188f27c522133f17bcfbd3c4cc9c0d2dd0653aa8a22678fbd9e0ec70e87a62" "q-19040/selection/f89dce3f749fcbecd74cfcf45917bb3f72c9e5d9702d9a02ba2a060b4187e84a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19040" :question/id #uuid "854d0f4a-8e08-5dc7-a816-ea56cbf65d2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-19040" :question/problem "Given that $g\\cdot h=8$, find the angle between $g=⟨t,t,t-1⟩$ and $h=⟨4,-2,-1⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, since $g\\cdot h=8$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =8 \\\\ t\\cdot 4+t\\cdot (-2)+(t-1)\\cdot (-1) & =8 \\\\ 4t-2t-t+1 & =8 \\\\ t+1 & =8 \\\\ t & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g & =⟨7,7,7-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,7,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $g$ and $h$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{g\\cdot h}{|\\,g\\,||\\,h\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{g}_{x}{h}_{x}+{g}_{y}{h}_{y}+{g}_{z}{h}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{g}_{x}^{2}+{g}_{y}^{2}+{g}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{h}_{x}^{2}+{h}_{y}^{2}+{h}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{134}\\cdot \\sqrt{21}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2\\,814}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2\\,814}})≈{81.33}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-19040/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19040"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-101512/selection/fdad1f8a9ae245b85e8d5bf8256ba7cc36a81d54412ee184a99721006622ab47" :answer/id #uuid "5a531894-930d-5aa8-be0a-b7eeb2655660" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101512/selection/494cd77ad8a9b447737f156e4d1a6455198b704f906ab2283374911afa938361" :answer/id #uuid "cd96dcf2-df7b-5d7d-b63a-2f885d7a0ef4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101512/selection/02ad3b4b6ef6cb24d617049ecf04ba873d5875bf1df0a09bf661f03e0714b5cc" :answer/id #uuid "fe092e6a-a292-562a-8e10-3a18cf911c21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{150}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101512/selection/4fea3101a12d72027d37d2702205342eaae6c8b446484d84e77543a2510dec4d" :answer/id #uuid "a6c459a6-1bf4-521f-b918-6d61ed3c3273" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101512/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a" :answer/id #uuid "9012605f-9225-5ab8-adaf-c6233a381fab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101512/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7d14433-e6bf-53f2-aba4-b6c9efded31e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101512/selection/4fea3101a12d72027d37d2702205342eaae6c8b446484d84e77543a2510dec4d" :answer-field/choices ["q-101512/selection/fdad1f8a9ae245b85e8d5bf8256ba7cc36a81d54412ee184a99721006622ab47" "q-101512/selection/494cd77ad8a9b447737f156e4d1a6455198b704f906ab2283374911afa938361" "q-101512/selection/02ad3b4b6ef6cb24d617049ecf04ba873d5875bf1df0a09bf661f03e0714b5cc" "q-101512/selection/4fea3101a12d72027d37d2702205342eaae6c8b446484d84e77543a2510dec4d" "q-101512/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101512" :question/id #uuid "0fe38227-7ce9-5330-a6c3-677c59d25bae" :question/math-academy-id "q-101512" :question/problem "Given that $a\\cdot b=-5$, find the angle between $a=⟨2t,t⟩$ and $b=⟨1,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $a\\cdot b=-5$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-5 \\\\ 2t\\cdot 1+t\\cdot 3 & =-5 \\\\ 2t+3t & =-5 \\\\ 5t & =-5 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨2(-1),\\,(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{5\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={135}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-101512/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101512"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4327"] :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{6} \\right) \\approx 111.9^\\circ.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4328"] :question/problem "Find $\\angle BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,-5)$, $B(-1,0,-4)$, and $C(5,1,1).$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,-5⟩,\\,b=⟨-1,0,-4⟩,\\,c=⟨5,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $\\angle BAC = \\theta.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-4⟩-⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩-⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{11}\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}} \\right) \\approx 92.5^\\circ.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5112"] :question/worked-solution "First, since $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-4 \\\\ t\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot t & =-4 \\\\ 6t-2t & =-4 \\\\ 4t & =-4 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨-1,-2⟩,\\,b=⟨6,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{37}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{185}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{4}{\\sqrt{185}} \\right) \\approx 107.1^\\circ.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
